What is the SMS Emden and what is its significance in history?
The SMS Emden was a German cruiser that played a significant role in World War I. It is significant in history because it was the first naval trophy of World War One from the Royal Australian Navy's first ship-to-ship battle, and one of only four salvaged from the SMS Emden. The Emden Gun, a salvaged gun from the SMS Emden, has state and national significance in Australia as a war trophy and memorial. Internationally, the battle between the SMS Emden and the HMAS Sydney is considered the most significant cruiser battle of World War I.
